# Charlie source files: Ruby is the closest existing Linguist language.
# Charlie's style is Ruby-influenced, so most syntax highlights cleanly
# (sigils like $foo and %sys won't be perfect; everything else mostly works).
# Replace with `linguist-language=Charlie` if/when Charlie lands in
# github-linguist proper.
*.charlie linguist-language=Ruby

# CharlieJSON files: JSON-shaped. Linguist would otherwise detect .cjs as
# CommonJS/JavaScript, which is wrong for this project.
*.cjs linguist-language=JSON
